skill: "vendor-spend-consolidator"
sections[3]:
  - "# vendor-spend-consolidator\n\nKeep one inventory of every software and hardware contract, surface renewals before they auto-renew, and propose consolidations where the same category is spread across multiple vendors. Use quarterly, when a renewal alert fires, or when spend in any category grows without a matching headcount or usage story.\n\nOwner: role-procurement-vendor-manager (pod-gna, procurement). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[5]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - search_web\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"billing ledger export from billing-automation; contract register from renewal-and-liability-watch; seat and license counts; hardware lease schedules\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/procurement/vendor-inventory.toon; renewal-calendar.toon with T-90 triggers; consolidation-memo.toon with savings estimates; lease-schedule.toon\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Merge the billing export with the contract register into one inventory; every recurring charge without a contract reference is flagged as unmanaged spend.\n2. Normalize each contract: vendor, category, seats or units, unit price, term end and notice window; normalize currencies to the functional currency with the rate and date recorded.\n3. Build the renewal calendar; every contract with a notice window gets a T-90 decision task so the window is exercised deliberately, not by autopay.\n4. Detect consolidation candidates: three or more vendors in one category, or duplicate capability flagged in the category taxonomy; list actual overlap evidence, not vendor-count alone.\n5. Estimate savings per consolidation with run_command using current unit prices; label estimates as estimates and name the data each one rests on.\n6. Track hardware leases in lease-schedule.toon with end-of-term options (return, buyout, extend) and the decision deadline for each.\n7. Emit ask_question for any consolidation that would move spend above the approval threshold or displace an incumbent with unexpired commitments.\n8. Write consolidation-memo.toon ranked by savings against effort; hand renewal decisions to the operator and new terms to role-contract-manager.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nrenewal notices to operators; negotiated terms to role-contract-manager.\n"
